From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:59:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: give every web app its uplink setting

The web player binds a web app's connections to the uplink in the
app's uplinkaddress setting, so every web app had to define that
setting and its strings itself. Kodi now defines it once, in
system/settings/webapp.xml with core strings: a web app that imports
kodi.webapp 1.3.0 gets Kodi's network category after its own
categories, or as its only one when it ships no settings.xml. The
values stay in the app's profile, so each app keeps its own uplink.

CWebApp adds the category through CAddon::LoadSettingsDefinition(),
where an add-on type can extend the definition it reads from the
add-on. A web app that defines a category or setting of Kodi's has no
settings then, as the log says, and the web player refuses to open it,
since it would ignore the uplink it is meant to use. Web apps that
import an older kodi.webapp keep the definition they ship.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
